  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Archive groups should have additional documentation created around them in order to let users know about their potential downsides in Fedora 6. Notably, versions of an object in OCFL are immutable, and purging a resource from an Archive Group results in a state where Fedora may say the resource doesn’t exist even though it still exists in OCFL.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
